`<img>` elements cause layout jumps because the browser doesn't know their dimensions until the image loads. Replacing them with `<div>` elements of fixed dimensions using `background-image` eliminates the reflow.

## Changes

- **`contentlist.jsx` / `card.jsx`** — Replace restaurant `<img>` tags with `<div role="img" aria-label={title}>` using inline `backgroundImage` style
- **`contentList.module.css`** — Replace `.main_content_item img` with `.img` class; add `height: 40px`, `flex-shrink: 0`, and background sizing/positioning properties
- **`card.module.css`** — Replace `.main_content img` with `.img` class; add `height: 165px`, `margin: auto` for centering, and background sizing/positioning properties

```jsx
// Before
<img src={restdb.image} alt={restdb.image} />

// After
<div
  className={s.img}
  style={{ backgroundImage: `url(${restdb.image})` }}
  aria-label={restdb.title}
  role="img"
/>
```

```css
/* Before */
.main_content img { width: 165px; /* no height */ }

/* After */
.img {
  width: 165px;
  height: 165px; /* fixed height prevents reflow */
  background-size: cover;
  background-position: center;
  background-repeat: no-repeat;
}
```

