Two UX issues: the main tab bar and server sub-tab bar scroll off screen when content is tall, and clicking "Add Server" produces no visible action unless the user discovers and checks a hidden SteamCMD checkbox.

## Tab layout — static tab bars, scrollable content panels

`##TabArea` now carries `NoScrollbar | NoScrollWithMouse`, pinning the main tab bar (Home / Server / Log) to the top permanently. The Home tab content is wrapped in its own `##HomeContent` scrollable child.

In `ServerTabWidget::render()`, each long-form sub-tab (Overview, Settings, Config, Mods, Backups) wraps its render call in a dedicated scrollable child, keeping the sub-tab bar visible at all times. Console and Logs already own their internal layout and are unchanged.

```cpp
// Before: entire ##TabArea (tabs + content) could scroll
ImGui::BeginChild("##TabArea");

// After: outer container is locked; each tab content scrolls independently
ImGui::BeginChild("##TabArea", ImVec2(0, 0), ImGuiChildFlags_None,
                  ImGuiWindowFlags_NoScrollbar | ImGuiWindowFlags_NoScrollWithMouse);
// ...
if (ImGui::BeginTabItem("Home", ...)) {
    ImGui::BeginChild("##HomeContent", ImVec2(0, 0));  // scrolls
    m_dashboard->render();
    ImGui::EndChild();
}
```

## Add Server — deploy on click

- `m_addInstallViaSteamCmd` now defaults to `true` when the dialog opens — SteamCMD deployment fires without requiring the user to find the checkbox.
- `std::filesystem::create_directories(s.dir)` is called unconditionally on Add, so the install directory is always provisioned. Failures are surfaced via both the log and a tray notification.

